# User state in /etc/xray, one name per line (file or directory): backup saves it to config/,
# restore takes it from a backup, deploy uploads what config/ has and install.sh puts it in place.
# This is the list of what a backup carries. What the panel's settings file carries is a different,
# larger list — /usr/share/flint/settings-files — because it also moves the modes and intervals that
# a backup keeps anyway. flint.env is here and not there on purpose: the PIN and the network stay
# with the router they belong to. tests/router/settings.sh checks that the two lists stay in step.
flint.env
nodes.conf
nodes-custom.conf
nodes.d
custom-sites
subscriptions
adblock-lists
adblock-rules
adblock-exclude
